{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere","id":581310,"title":"Tremere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-06T11:53:46-07:00","id":581310,"title":"Tremere","content":"Hi everyone!<br /> <br /> I was wondering, has anyone done anything with Tremere from V;tM? I thought they were awesome! Essentially vampire mages with the their discipline (can't remember the name) limited only by their imagination! I checked the Homebrew sticky, and tI haven't noticed anything there.<br /> <br /> Just curious. I thought they were pretty nifty <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Thaumaturgy, that's it =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","user":"Krzyzstof","date":".  KNOWLEDGE!! 07-06-2015, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:11:26-07:00","id":581353,"title":"","content":"I nailed together some Tremere, who were basically a cross-over faction within the Ordo Dracul and Invictus.<br /> <br /> I think they worked out fairly well, although the Path of Blood I used (a slightly updated version of the Translation guide Thaumaturgy) is incredibly broken with the new Frenzy rules.<br /> I also sketched out path of levinbolt and conjuring, and am contemplating a version of countermagic.<br /> <br /> Haven't posted anything on the homebrew stuff though, since my PoB is basically the one from the Translation guide, and the others are not of showable quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:14:37-07:00","id":581361,"title":"","content":"Officially Tremere are now a Mage legacy of soul devouring awakened. As for VtR substitutes, Circle of Crone or even Lancea Sanctum can play their role pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:19:06-07:00","id":581367,"title":"","content":"The Tremere in nWod are a Mage subgroup, often referred to as Liches. The best writeup of them can be found in Left-Handed Path: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/107263/LeftHand-Path\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/.../LeftHand-Path</a><br /> <br /> As for cWoD conversions I'd point you towards the Vampire Translation Guide (<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/86202/Vampire-Translation-Guide\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...nslation-Guide</a>) or Yossarian's 13 Licks (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke#post5268\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...smoke#post5268</a>) as starting points. Thaumaturgy itself can be adapted either from Vampire's Blood Magic Disciplines or by cribbing spells from Mage the Awakening, or both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:28:36-07:00","id":581376,"title":"","content":"Awesome, thanks everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I shall definitely check those out.<br /> <br /> Seidmadr, I would definitely like to check those out at some point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Side note, weren't Liches in cWoD as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:31:52-07:00","id":581377,"title":"","content":"Also, just looked at the description of Left-Hand. That's pretty much what my Malkav was trying to do. Raise his own watch tower.. I might finally be able to find out how! Muwahahahaha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:35:00-07:00","id":581383,"title":"","content":"While mechanical reasons to not want the Tremere are less interesting than thematic ones, I think it's worth pointing out that the Sanctified and the Circle both do blood mages with a bit more character, and having an entire clan whose only hat is &quot;Hermetic Wizards&quot; is a bit narrow for a Clan concept.<br /> <br /> If I were gonna make Tremere as Vampires, I'd probably give them a different name, reference the Tremere Liches in their backstory, and focus on making their magic distinctive and less catch-all. Maybe try to bring more Hermeticism into it? I dunno. The whole DnD wizard schtick for vampires is awkward, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:42:35-07:00","id":581387,"title":"","content":"That is a very interesting idea. Maybe the Liches managed to raise their tower. There was a power feud afterwards and one of the 'factions' broke off and went for the more undead thing instead of the mage thing. Just the first thought to pop off my brain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:47:44-07:00","id":581388,"title":"","content":"Left-Handed Path has a whole history for the Tremere which, while suitably vague, is highly suggestive of many setting elements. There was a period where they were, very probably, vampires and slaves to something called the Theban, then later broke away via the sixth Watch Tower and became (for a time) reaper hunters to disguise their own nature. There's a lot more, but it's all very interesting, the whole book really.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, check the Son's of Phobos in Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies (<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/105095/Blood-Sorcery-Sacraments--Blasphemies\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...s--Blasphemies</a>) another good resource for Tremere-like factions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:51:47-07:00","id":581391,"title":"","content":"Or that original Tremere Bloodline Kindred survived Abyssal Intrusion remaking the mages in to the Liches they are in <b>Mage</b>. Those (vampire) Tremere went to hiding for centuries, afraid of the bastards that become Soul Reapers and incorporated almost every other Reaper school in to them. Vampiric Tremere returned as secret faction inside Ordo Dracul that want's to take back at the Liches in Awakened society, come over for vampiric aptheosis and world domination, muahahahahah! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-06-2015, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:58:53-07:00","id":581395,"title":"","content":"I plan to use them as a Mekhet bloodline, so far I have the following:<br /> <b>Nickname:</b> diabolists.<br /> <b>Disciplines: </b> Auspex, Celerity, Obfuscate, Sanguinem Miracula.<br /> <b>Bloodline bane:</b> hierarchy is innate to the blood of the Tremere. Each drink towards a Vinculum counts as two, and the Tremere may not intentionally betray anybody they have even a first stage bond towards.<br /> <br /> Their history is generally the same as in the oWoD, except without the status as betrayers. I plan to give Sanguinem Miracula powers based off of the path of blood, and state that the user can also learn and use rituals as for Cruac and Theban sorcery (while providing a handful).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T16:38:21-07:00","id":581692,"title":"","content":"I have used them before as a bloodline or a covenant. As a bloodline they are a part from clan Mekhet whose bloodline discipline is Breath, which I can't remember right now where it's from. They favor the Ordo Dracul due to the covenant's philosophy and teachings, though they greatly despise the Lancea Sanctum and the Invictus due to past history with them. <br /> <br /> As a covenant they accept all the clans and their covenant discipline is Thaumaturgy rite. Their sort of like the Ordo Dracul except they mean to find magical knowledge that would increase the covenant's occult teachings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T21:13:34-07:00","id":581924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=581353#post581353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I nailed together some Tremere,</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember trying to nail some Tremere together. Should have used bigger nails...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T23:30:40-07:00","id":581992,"title":"","content":"More thinking of Tremere vampires in new World of Darkness, I would make them <b>both</b> Ordo Dracul secret faction and Mekhet Bloodline. From the Mage <b>Left Hand Path, </b> Tremere Liches lore says they were slaves to Theban that made some mages in to Breath-Eaters - vampires surviving by breath, not blood.<br /> <br /> As this, I would make those that survived the massacre by Liches to finally be freed from Theban slavery and become Mekhet Bloodline with special Discipline of Blood usage ( maybe called <i>Sanguine</i>, or something ), with final power of surviving on Breath, not Blood - five different powers per Discipline in <b>Requiem</b> 2ED are still a thing? I would give them some power over Blood Bonds, Blood usage and finally, on living on Breath of victims. They were see as threat to some Kindred from similarities of they powers to those of the Strix and their feeding habits.<br /> <br /> Our Tremere Bloodline would gone in to secrecy by centuries, developing more and more Blood Sorcery they stolen from Theban ( <b><i>not</i></b> their Disicpilne ) and when Ordo Dracul come to being, they infiltrated it and make a large secret faction in Dragons secret society. Now, Tremere Kindred are Ordo Dracul that practice their Blood Sorcery and have very antagonistic views on Lancea et Sanctum ( and probably Invictus ) - but, mainly, they want to dwell in to mages society to uncover Tremere Liches and plan, after centuries in hiding, to take care Awakened soul-eating parasites that almost killed the millenia before. They are Ordo's faction dedicated to contacts with mages, inflirtrating Orders in secret to uncover Thremere Liches in them.<br /> <br /> Damn, I now need to remade mine NPC Ordo Dracul Prince of the London as the part of Tremere sect and throw in to our <b>Mage</b> game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=581692#post581692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a covenant they accept all the clans and their covenant discipline is Thaumaturgy rite. Their sort of like the Ordo Dracul except they mean to find magical knowledge that would increase the covenant's occult teachings.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do not feel to me as whole Covenant, or that different from Ordo Dracul to make them really new Covenant onto itself. They will work better now as faction admits the Dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-07-2015, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T02:05:12-07:00","id":582056,"title":"","content":"I haven't personally read <i>Left Hand Path</i>, but it seems like there could be some significance to the Theban's name. Theban Sorcery, or something like it, existed long before the birth of Jesus, much less the founding of the Lancea et Sanctum; maybe the Theban is a blood-sorcerer who introduced Sorcery to the Sanctified. The Theban itself seems to have evolved into something unique and altogether different from ordinary vampires, implying that it kept its most potent secrets to itself.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the &quot;true&quot; Tremere are a group of vampires who have been adopted as disciples by the Theban and entrusted with blood magic different from and potentially more potent than that wielded by the Sanctified. This needn't break game balance; their powers could be on par with those of Theban Sorcerers, but divorced from the trappings of Christianity and laden with the vague promise of more incredible secrets waiting to be uncovered. They might exist as a hidden sect within the Lancea et Sanctum (who have an academic side that isn't always appreciated), but actually put their faith in some kind of pseudo-Hermetic mystery cult (since, after all, the original Tremere came out of the Order of Hermes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-07-2015, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T03:35:08-07:00","id":582097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=582056#post582056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might exist as a hidden sect within the Lancea et Sanctum (who have an academic side that isn't always appreciated), but actually put their faith in some kind of pseudo-Hermetic mystery cult (since, after all, the original Tremere came out of the Order of Hermes).</div> </div> </div> </div>Does not the Ordo Dracul is based on quasi-Hermetic ideology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T07:22:39-07:00","id":582245,"title":"","content":"My idea for the Tremere is to keep them as sorcerers with their own form of blood magic and make them into a Clan that was created by the Strix throught a nightmarish pact with, unpleasent, human occultists and mystics. At least that's how I'll run them if I shall run Vampire Dark Ages in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T07:57:19-07:00","id":582290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=582245#post582245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea for the Tremere is to keep them as sorcerers with their own form of blood magic and make them into a Clan that was created by the Strix throught a nightmarish pact with, unpleasent, human occultists and mystics. At least that's how I'll run them if I shall run Vampire Dark Ages in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not a bloodline? An actually unique discipline, came into being under 1000 years ago, transformed themselves using the blood of vampires, these all sound like strong hints of being a bloodline to me.<br /> <br /> To be fair though, I'm statting them up alongside a couple of homebrew Ordo Dracul disciplines now (one for warding, and one for holding) because they seem like a good fit for a fringe part of the covenant. They are the only practitioners of proper Blood Sorcery in the covenant, but lack access to some parts of the Coils (In essence they can't have any Coil above Status (Ordo Dracul) and difficulty learning Scales). Being connected to the Strix is a really good idea, what if a Strix uplifted the first Tremere from Revenants after their sireless embrace? It gives a reason for them to be mistrusted by other Kindred, because the Strix have yet to collect on their end of the bargain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T09:29:50-07:00","id":582433,"title":"","content":"A Tremere style (Hermetic Wizards) Meket Shadow Cult would also work well. Claiming descent from the original Sorcerers of Thebes, these &quot;True Thebans&quot; would recruit mortal occultists to assist in their rituals and mask their presence behind secret societies like the Hermetic Order of the Golden Dawn.<br /> <br /> Shadow Cult (True Thebans) Initiation<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>*</b></span> Gain a &quot;Hermeticism&quot; specialty in the Occult Skill<br /> *** Gain access to Theban Sorcery Rituals regardless of Covenant (Lance members cannot be part of cult)<br /> ***** Gain a three dot Occult Library Merit representing access to the inner secrets of the cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T15:56:57-07:00","id":582828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=582290#post582290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not a bloodline? An actually unique discipline, came into being under 1000 years ago, transformed themselves using the blood of vampires, these all sound like strong hints of being a bloodline to me.<br /> <br /> To be fair though, I'm statting them up alongside a couple of homebrew Ordo Dracul disciplines now (one for warding, and one for holding) because they seem like a good fit for a fringe part of the covenant. They are the only practitioners of proper Blood Sorcery in the covenant, but lack access to some parts of the Coils (In essence they can't have any Coil above Status (Ordo Dracul) and difficulty learning Scales). Being connected to the Strix is a really good idea, what if a Strix uplifted the first Tremere from Revenants after their sireless embrace? It gives a reason for them to be mistrusted by other Kindred, because the Strix have yet to collect on their end of the bargain.</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough, and I'm happy you like the Strix part. My only defense is that the idea is to have them exist in the DAV universe and thus more narrow concepts for clans are the norm, as well as not as many bloodlines.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T21:29:26-07:00","id":583167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=581992#post581992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More thinking of Tremere vampires in new World of Darkness, I would make them <b>both</b> Ordo Dracul secret faction and Mekhet Bloodline. From the Mage <b>Left Hand Path, </b> Tremere Liches lore says they were slaves to Theban that made some mages in to Breath-Eaters - vampires surviving by breath, not blood.<br /> <br /> As this, I would make those that survived the massacre by Liches to finally be freed from Theban slavery and become Mekhet Bloodline with special Discipline of Blood usage ( maybe called <i>Sanguine</i>, or something ), with final power of surviving on Breath, not Blood - five different powers per Discipline in <b>Requiem</b> 2ED are still a thing? I would give them some power over Blood Bonds, Blood usage and finally, on living on Breath of victims. They were see as threat to some Kindred from similarities of they powers to those of the Strix and their feeding habits.<br /> <br /> Our Tremere Bloodline would gone in to secrecy by centuries, developing more and more Blood Sorcery they stolen from Theban ( <b><i>not</i></b> their Disicpilne ) and when Ordo Dracul come to being, they infiltrated it and make a large secret faction in Dragons secret society. Now, Tremere Kindred are Ordo Dracul that practice their Blood Sorcery and have very antagonistic views on Lancea et Sanctum ( and probably Invictus ) - but, mainly, they want to dwell in to mages society to uncover Tremere Liches and plan, after centuries in hiding, to take care Awakened soul-eating parasites that almost killed the millenia before. They are Ordo's faction dedicated to contacts with mages, inflirtrating Orders in secret to uncover Thremere Liches in them.<br /> <br /> Damn, I now need to remade mine NPC Ordo Dracul Prince of the London as the part of Tremere sect and throw in to our <b>Mage</b> game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They do not feel to me as whole Covenant, or that different from Ordo Dracul to make them really new Covenant onto itself. They will work better now as faction admits the Dragons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used the vampire translation guide and after my group played the covenant and got deeper into there philosophy it kind of seem similar to the Ordo Dracul. Plus Thaumaturgy Rite played a perfect disciplne for the covenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:52:12-07:00","id":583705,"title":"","content":"I'd recommend they use a secular version of veneficia. They could be like old hermetic semioticians. It's not Theban sorcery, but it's still based on intellect and academics. Unlike the Setites, Cappadocians etc, I could never see what the Tremere were trying to accomplish beyond survival through magic by making themselves important and indispensable. So I see them <i>within</i> Invictus i.e. the biggest, meanest ally that has least reason to hate them. After all, they make themselves useful through providing magical solutions and if other covenants can do that, there's a problem. I also quite like the idea of them being Ventrue-wannabe Mekhet as the Players are to Daeva.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:19:50-07:00","id":584825,"title":"","content":"OWoD Tremere were heavily overpowered with no real clan weakness.<br /> If I were to bring them back they would have a secular version of Theban. It is more hermetic than venficia or which is just a form of cruac.<br /> Clan is tricky to me Maybe mekhet or maybe a Covenant. That is the problem for me. As a Clan the original lacked flavour.<br /> The old version has two clan specials and their own clan special. They don't really scream clan to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T13:25:05-07:00","id":585069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=584825#post584825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OWoD Tremere were heavily overpowered with no real clan weakness.<br /> If I were to bring them back they would have a secular version of Theban. It is more hermetic than venficia or which is just a form of cruac.<br /> Clan is tricky to me Maybe mekhet or maybe a Covenant. That is the problem for me. As a Clan the original lacked flavour.<br /> The old version has two clan specials and their own clan special. They don't really scream clan to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's why I suggested a Shadow Cult. The only down side to that is the Shadow cults are supposed to be secret societies / conspiracies, so they couldn't be a &quot;public&quot; part of kindred society. If you want other kindred to know about them, they'd need to be a minor covenant or a notorious branch of the Ordo Dracul focused on using ritual/hermetic magic as part of their quest for transcendence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:04:18-07:00","id":585175,"title":"","content":"Where are described Shadow Cults of Requiem? In 2ED corebook? They sound interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:39:50-07:00","id":585232,"title":"","content":"They're in the Mekhet clanbook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T16:07:49-07:00","id":585316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=584825#post584825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is more hermetic than venficia or which is just a form of cruac.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Where Cr\u00faac is dark and mystifying, Venercia are exacting and logical&quot;<br /> <br /> The power probably comes from the same place, but the execution demands a completely different mental discipline. I think extending Theban Sorcery would detract from its mystery (so I'd probably run the Architects of the Monolith a bit differently, much as I like them). As I recall, Thaumaturgy isn't fundamentally that different from other blood magics like Setite sorceries, it's just a different paradigm. Veneficia could be seen as a form of theurgy dependent on the alchemical properties of vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:09:22-07:00","id":585609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=585175#post585175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are described Shadow Cults of Requiem? In 2ED corebook? They sound interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They are interesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> They were introduced in the Mekhet clan book, and seem to be the inspiration for the Conspiracies in The Danse Macabre and Hunter: The Vigil. They probably also inspired the Mystery Cult Initiation merit in GM and B&amp;S.<br /> <br /> The core concept was based on the idea of Mekhet building secret societies as a means of bringing mortals under their influence despite lacking mind bending powers like Dominate or Majesty. Initiation into the cult was racked via an escalating merit, which brought bonuses based on the themes the cult was built around. Shadow Cults have three levels of initiation. Humans could be brought into the first level of the cult, from which they would serve as food or minions. The Mekhet clan book has a bunch of additional rules for having a character go through the process of building such a cult for themselves to lead.<br /> <br /> Rendered more like a Mystery Cult, the Tremere might <span style=\"font-size:14px\">be...</span><br /> <br /> A story is told among the Magi of the Atlantean traditions. It is story of eager Mages seduced and betrayed by the cursed undead. A story of vampires who drank souls and who destroyed themselves by attempting to consume Mages. Magi who were then left corrupted by the treacherous assault. Needless to say, the Kindred heirs of House Tremere tell a very different version of the tale.<br /> <br /> In the vampire's account it was they who were betrayed. A wise kindred mystic named Tremere and his students had spent centuries studying the mystic arts to find a means of alleviating their cursed condition. They were approached by a group of Mages who promised to share their mystical knowledge and aid in the search for a cure for vampirism. Though the mages shared many secrets, their altruism was a mask hiding a sinister agenda. The magi hoped to use their arcane arts to steal the immortality of the Kindred, and once the vampires dropped their guard, the Mages struck.<br /> <br /> Tremere was laid low, cast into permanent Torpor by mystic means. Most of his followers were tortured to death in the Mages' experiments, as the Magi used the power of the Kindred curse to transmute themselves into immortals. All was not lost, however, for a few of Tremere's apprentices survived. The Magi had taught the Kindred too many of their secrets, and the followers of Tremere were able to summon powerful elemental spirits to their aid. In a single night of sorcerous fury the power of Kindred blood joined with the essence of the shadow realm to overcome Atlantean arcana. The magi were driven from house Tremere, and the Torpid form of the house's founded was reclaimed.<br /> <br /> Tonight, most of the followers of Tremere have given up the quest for a cure. Instead they hold an endless vigil over his body, and constantly study the occult in a ceaseless mission to find a way to revive him. Their ancient pacts with the great elemental lords still hold; granting them both power and protection. The grounds of the Chapter houses of the Cult of Tremere are guarded by earth elementals and golems, who can crush most intruders with ease. While the halls within are patrolled by invisible spirits of air and shadow, who lead unwelcome visitors astray. In battle the Tremere wield powerful amulets which direct the power of the spirits against their enemies. The mightiest of the Tremere even summon and bind beings of living flame, to unleash upon Kindred foes.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>*</b></span> Tremere initiates are schooled in the art of &quot;Hermetic Theurgy&quot;, the evoking of spirits for knowledge and power. They gain a free &quot;Spirits&quot; specialty in Occult.<br /> <br /> ** Tremere Apprentices who have proven themselves are introduced to the cults network of occult scholars. They gain the Contacts Merit (Occultists) free of charge.<br /> <br /> *** As a Tremere experiments with Hermetic rituals and undergoes further cult initiations they become attuned to the spirit world. They gain the Unseen Senses Merit pertaining to Spirits for free.<br /> <br /> **** Highly proficient in handling spirits, high ranked Tremere manifest the ability to converse with spirits and perform summon rituals with little preparation. They gain the Medium Merit pertaining to Spirits for free.<br /> <br /> ***** Just as powerful spirits become renown among occultists, so to do power full occultists become renowned among spirits. The Archons of the Tremere have the equivalent of a three dot Fame Merit among spirits, granting them a +3 bonus when attempting to communicate with and influence spirit entities.<br /> <br /> (see The God Machine Chronicle for references on spirits and supernatural merits)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","user":"Vyrkolash","date":". 07-10-2015, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:11:14-07:00","id":585620,"title":"","content":"I echo the sentiments that the Tremere would probably fit best as a Shadow Cult, In order to better fit their original mythos from cWoD, I would suggest making them a former group of Mages that perhaps were tricked by the Strix into witnessing a terrifying false vision of the Exarchs' victory and Magic's demise in the Fallen World. The Tremere could have stumbled upon either a Strix powerful enough to serve as their patron, or that the patron of Kindred (the Crone or something else entirely) and decided that, as Kindred, their blood magick would be safely outside the influence of Exarchs<br /> <br /> They discovered how to surgically remove their Ka and proceeded to embrace themselves through stolen Vitae and very Ordo Dracul-esque procedures. Ah Tremere, how I miss your almost secular blood magic... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T02:05:20-07:00","id":585780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=585620#post585620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah Tremere, how I miss your almost secular blood magic... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably go for making them a Mekhet bloodline exclusive to the Ordo Dracul, too, Maybe founded by an apostate Acolyte who took profound knowledge of Cr\u00faac with him/her when joining the Ordo Dracul. Hidden away from the vengeful eyes of the Circle, they analyzed Cr\u00faac and organized it into a rigid system of hermetic tradition. The resulting Thaumaturgy is a form of blood sorcery that feels <i>almost</i> sterile and scientific.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T19:37:15-07:00","id":589797,"title":"","content":"Okay, so this might go into the realmt of 'off the rail' lunacy\u2014or at least APPEAR to do\u2014and I apologise before hand. Please don't read further if you'd rather not see wonky changes that are not fully explained, deprived of much context, and reliant on thoughts that I won't fully share here. With that out of the way, here's what I got:<br /> <br /> In MY version, the House of Tremere is a Covenant with a history mirroring that of the Ordo Dracul. The Dragons and the Tremere grew out of very old rites and applications of Will over Vitae, but where Dracula took a secular and logical approach to building his Mysteries, the Kindred who became Tremere sought only power. The inherent paradox of a Covenant of power-hungry blood wizards is the exact reason why the Covenant needs their strict and draconian Pyramid structure, one where every Magus knows his place within their Black Academy. These vampire wizards use their elemental Paths of Power as arcane means for turning the latent potencies of Vitae into useful effects, but any Tremere Magus knows that raw power needs focus. Most use Sendings to focus their Paths, allowing them to create subtler, more predicable results.<br /> <br /> ...Now, in <i>mechanical</i> terms, Tremere 'Thaumaturgy' does a lot of what the Ordo Dracul's Mysteries do, with Paths taking the place of Coils, Sendings acting in a way like Scales. There ARE differences, and the most important is the outward directed, elemental nature of Thaumaturgy Paths versus the inward and transcendent Coils of the Dragon. Hence, the end results also vary considerably, as a Magus cares nothing for fairytales of 'transcendence' or any similar guff. Thaumaturgy is all about power, and power deserves to exist in THIS world, not some far-off post-mortality wonderland. Finally, the approach is quite different between the two, with the occult taking centre stage for the Tremere. Oh sure, he'll use science and academia when he must, but to the eyes of a Magus, a Dragon is a slave to her procedures and 'repeatable results' and all that nonsense. To gain power, a Magus must risk much.<br /> <br /> My reason for adding this had less to do with wanting Warlocks in <b>Requiem</b> and far more with giving the Ordo Dracul a more refined and well stated sense of direction. The Dragons have a very steady, rational approach in most of their work, but in the Ordo Dracul book especially, I saw this very jarring juxtaposition of the occult and the scientific. I wanted a more pure magical society of Kindred, and the Tremere appeared a good fit. I decided that Dracula didn't <i>invent</i> the Coils, but after he found texts and practitioners of older schools of blood manipulation, old Prince Vlad perfected those notions (read: Coils of the Dragon as they appear in First Edition) into the Mysteries that we know today. Another group, possibly with connexion to the 'founders' of the Left Hand Tremere Liches, took those same base philosophies and rites into a much more mystical direction...<br /> <br /> There's a LOT more that I've written about this, and my troupe's been playtesting my homebrew Thaumaturgy\u2014as mentioned above, the straight conversion you'll find the <i>Vampire Translation Guide</i> is CRAZY over-powered for <b>Requiem</b>. I'm not saying that my version is anything that's worth adding to your game, but it's been fun at my table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T11:14:44-07:00","id":590310,"title":"","content":"I thought about this too when I first use the vampire translation guide. But when it came to Tremere paths I didn't like it cause it felt like I was still playing V:tM. I wanted to make the Tremere covenant look original in Requiem so instead I just used Thaumaturgy Rites as the covenant's discipline, which worked beautifully and yeah, the Tremere covenant does feel similar to the Ordo Dracul except Tremere focuses on occult power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T16:47:25-07:00","id":590583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=590310#post590310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought about this too when I first use the vampire translation guide. But when it came to Tremere paths I didn't like it cause it felt like I was still playing V:tM. I wanted to make the Tremere covenant look original in Requiem so instead I just used Thaumaturgy Rites as the covenant's discipline, which worked beautifully and yeah, the Tremere covenant does feel similar to the Ordo Dracul except Tremere focuses on occult power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ordo Dracul also fill the Occult Power niche <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Even more so than the other covenants, since they specifically look at it from the power advantage angle. Anyways...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T21:57:12-07:00","id":590846,"title":"","content":"That is true. Some of the coils are power bases. It makes the vampire seem almost indestructible when removing their weaknesses and finding new ways to accaquire new powers. I guess I still have that mentality of them being these occult scientists who's only objective is to rid vampire weakness/flaws. The Tremere covenant, however, I see them as these vampire wizards who are trying to gain occult knowledge/power in order to enhance vampirism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T22:06:51-07:00","id":590869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=590846#post590846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is true. Some of the coils are power bases. It makes the vampire seem almost indestructible when removing their weaknesses and finding new ways to accaquire new powers. I guess I still have that mentality of them being these occult scientists who's only objective is to rid vampire weakness/flaws. <b>The Tremere covenant, however, I see them as these vampire wizards who are trying to gain occult knowledge/power in order to enhance vampirism.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That part is Ordo Dracul description basically copy pasted from the book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T22:29:45-07:00","id":590893,"title":"","content":"And this is why I totally think Tremere works as secret faction inside the Ordo Dracul. The &quot;power hungry occultists&quot; faction to be precise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T23:09:18-07:00","id":590953,"title":"","content":"Well, Phoalan I'd like to see more, especially the mechanics, for the Tremere. I like your description of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T06:11:38-07:00","id":591210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=590893#post590893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is why I totally think Tremere works as secret faction inside the Ordo Dracul. The &quot;power hungry occultists&quot; faction to be precise. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Ordo Dracul applies scientific principles to Blood Magic, and the Tremere come around, nick the basics of the techniques, craft them into something more magicy (coil of the ascendant goes from becoming resistant to flames and the sun to controlling fire. Ideally rather poorly) and then slap on some mystic bullshit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T06:31:13-07:00","id":591216,"title":"","content":"The conceptual difference between the Tremere and the Odo Dracul isn't superstition vs science. The Tremere were mystics, but research and experimentation were part of their mystical learning process. The Ordo is a secret society with a mystical mission and pseudo-scientific methodologies reminiscent of parapsychology and victorian era spiritualism. The typical dragon has more in common with Dr. Frankenstein than with Albert Einstein.<br /> <br /> Both groups study the occult, and both rationalize their approach. The difference between them is that the Tremere cultivate control over the world around them, while the Ordo develops control over their own state of being. The Tremere make sense as part of the Ordo if they are considered renegades or degenerates. Mainstream Dragons would view them with mistrust or disappointment, because they &quot;lost the mission&quot; by focusing on cultivating mystical power rather than overcoming the curse. At best they might be seen as a necessary evil, if they make themselves useful by helping to secure Wyrms' nests or fighting other covenants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T07:37:00-07:00","id":591289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=591216#post591216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both groups study the occult, and both rationalize their approach. The difference between them is that the Tremere cultivate control over the world around them, while the Ordo develops control over their own state of being. The Tremere make sense as part of the Ordo if they are considered renegades or degenerates. Mainstream Dragons would view them with mistrust or disappointment, because they &quot;lost the mission&quot; by focusing on cultivating mystical power rather than overcoming the curse. At best they might be seen as a necessary evil, if they make themselves useful by helping to secure Wyrms' nests or fighting other covenants.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why Temere makes so nice inside Faction - on first glace they seem to work with Ordo goals. But more you go deeper, you see those participants would work like secret society inside secret society of Dracul - great faction to use in your game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T09:10:44-07:00","id":591393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=591289#post591289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's why Temere makes so nice inside Faction - on first glace they seem to work with Ordo goals. But more you go deeper, you see those participants would work like secret society inside secret society of Dracul - great faction to use in your game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair point, that would make them like the Sworn of the Ladder or the Sworn of the Locust. Come to think of it the Ordo Dracul covenant book does describe one of the &quot;Transcendental Camps&quot; (the schools of thought within the order) as &quot;Liches&quot; who believe transcendence is about having ever increasing control over oneself <i>and the rest of the world</i>. The Tremere could function as followers and champions of that philosophy. Sort of a &quot;Sworn of the Pyramid&quot; faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T11:01:00-07:00","id":591536,"title":"","content":"In Reqiuem, they feel more suitable as a bloodline, that's my opinion. Having the whole history with the Theban and the Tremere Lich makes them sound like they were once a bloodline, or still are. I hope in the near future OP can make a supplement that dwells deeper into the Tremere Lich's history. I'm really eager to know more about Theban.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T11:32:00-07:00","id":591581,"title":"","content":"I still more in favor of <b>both</b> the Ordo Dracul faction and original Breath Stealers Bloodline. But <b>not</b> the Covenant on to itself - Tremere are too limited in scope to compete with other fives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:41:21-07:00","id":591721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=591581#post591581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still more in favor of <b>both</b> the Ordo Dracul faction and original Breath Stealers Bloodline. But <b>not</b> the Covenant on to itself - Tremere are too limited in scope to compete with other fives.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I liked most of the minor covenants in The Danse Macabre. Introducing the Tremere as a minor covenant (formerly based in Austria but now scattered as a result of persecution at the hands of the Third Reich) could be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T20:34:26-07:00","id":592261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=591721#post591721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I liked most of the minor covenants in The Danse Macabre. Introducing the Tremere as a minor covenant (formerly based in Austria but now scattered as a result of persecution at the hands of the Third Reich) could be fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh they are fun. When I played them as a covenant they were toe to toe against the Ordo Dracul. Both of them wanted to steal each others occult knowledge and prove they were superior to each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T03:56:59-07:00","id":592475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=591216#post591216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conceptual difference between the Tremere and the Odo Dracul isn't superstition vs science. The Tremere were mystics, but research and experimentation were part of their mystical learning process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the Tremere as taking the Discworld approach to their powers: dress it up in mysticism so everybody thinks it's harder than it is. When they research they are still as Scientific as the Ordo, but they then dress it up in mumbo jumbo and pretend it's even more difficult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Ordo is a secret society with a mystical mission and pseudo-scientific methodologies reminiscent of parapsychology and victorian era spiritualism. The typical dragon has more in common with Dr. Frankenstein than with Albert Einstein. </div> </div> </div>Nothing in the book implies that Victor Frankenstein was a bad scientist. He used alchemy and didn't repeat his experiment, but that was partially due to the attitudes of his time, and his experiment was the result of at least months of research. I see the doctor as a good example of what an Ordo Dracul researcher should be: a long time spent researching and gathering materials until he finally tries the experiment that will prove his theory works. If you wanted to create a patchwork person and create it by the way, I'd suggest Coil of the Voivode as the basis for such a scale.<br /> <br /> Also, the amount of science and pseudoscience will change depending on the specific vampire, I have younger members working in groups and using less pseudoscience in order to conduct research that takes longer, but is much more likely to produce useful results. The older members of the covenant don't really see it as real research, to which the neonates respond that the world has moved on, and can you please explain what Mr Magus meant by 'align the crystals in a counterclockwise rotation towards the orbit of mercury?' You still get the oddity and psudeoscience is more common than real science, but the covenant is changing, slowly, and is only slightly more out of touch with the modern world than the Carthians.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Both groups study the occult, and both rationalize their approach. The difference between them is that the Tremere cultivate control over the world around them, while the Ordo develops control over their own state of being. The Tremere make sense as part of the Ordo if they are considered renegades or degenerates. Mainstream Dragons would view them with mistrust or disappointment, because they &quot;lost the mission&quot; by focusing on cultivating mystical power rather than overcoming the curse. At best they might be seen as a necessary evil, if they make themselves useful by helping to secure Wyrms' nests or fighting other covenants. </div> </div> </div>I agree with this, but I would say that they study the occult with a mix of science and pseudoscience, and the Ordo would prefer to downplay the role pseudoscience has in it. The Ordo does occasionally admit that the Coils probably are a strange form of blood magic, but they prefer to promote the Science side, just hide the other 70%. The Tremere prefer to say that they use rigorously developed magic in my version, and throw a few crystals, skulls, stuffed crocodiles and pentagrams into the mix to convince the other vampires that it can't be done with three short sticks and 4cc of mouse blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T08:32:04-07:00","id":592651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=592475#post592475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see the Tremere as taking the Discworld approach to their powers: dress it up in mysticism so everybody thinks it's harder than it is. When they research they are still as Scientific as the Ordo, but they then dress it up in mumbo jumbo and pretend it's even more difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love that approach to 'secular' mystics. Frankly, I think it fits the Ordo as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=592475#post592475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in the book implies that Victor Frankenstein was a bad scientist. He used alchemy and didn't repeat his experiment, but that was partially due to the attitudes of his time, and his experiment was the result of at least months of research. I see the doctor as a good example of what an Ordo Dracul researcher should be: a long time spent researching and gathering materials until he finally tries the experiment that will prove his theory works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't criticizing Dr. Frankenstein (and I can't imagine saying that anywhere but a WOD forum) I was just invoking him as a fantastic example of an Ordo &quot;scientist&quot; compared to a stereotypical scientist. As you point out his approach, as described by Shelley, reflects the ideas of the time. That's significant because most elders in the covenant would be from that time or earlier, so those same ideas would be prominent in their thinking. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=592475#post592475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the amount of science and pseudoscience will change depending on the specific vampire, I have younger members working in groups and using less pseudoscience in order to conduct research that takes longer, but is much more likely to produce useful results. The older members of the covenant don't really see it as real research, to which the neonates respond that the world has moved on, and can you please explain what Mr Magus meant by 'align the crystals in a counterclockwise rotation towards the orbit of mercury?' You still get the oddity and psudeoscience is more common than real science, but the covenant is changing, slowly, and is only slightly more out of touch with the modern world than the Carthians.<br /> <br /> ... they study the occult with a mix of science and pseudoscience, and the Ordo would prefer to downplay the role pseudoscience has in it. The Ordo does occasionally admit that the Coils probably are a strange form of blood magic, but they prefer to promote the Science side, just hide the other 70%. The Tremere prefer to say that they use rigorously developed magic in my version, and throw a few crystals, skulls, stuffed crocodiles and pentagrams into the mix to convince the other vampires that it can't be done with three short sticks and 4cc of mouse blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>The disparities between science, pseudoscience, and mysticism are less clear cut than most people think. All are attempts to explain the world via internally consistent systems of thought. The real difference is just the assumptions you are allowed to make when formulating theories, and the language you use to describe said theories. Secular skeptics claim science makes no assumptions, but in reality it assume the absence of the supernatural. Pseudoscience uses the language of science, but is willing to make limited assumptions about the presence and relevance of supernatural influences (often while denying their supernatural nature). Mysticism tends to assume the significance of supernatural influences, makes untestable claims about the nature of such influences, and uses archaic language to describe such influences.<br /> <br /> For example, a Crone cultist assumes their goddess is what grants power to their blood magic. A Dragon pseudoscientist accepts that blood magic works, but either doesn't claim to know what powers it or describes the power source in terms of &quot;energy&quot;. A scientist assumes blood magic is impossible and must be some kind of trickery. The problem in the WOD is obvious; the scientist is wrong. A Dragon, as a vampire who frequents haunted houses and spirit loci, does not have the luxury of being a strict scientist. <br /> <br /> When Mr Magus tells his students to meditate in a circle of crystals aligned &quot;in a counterclockwise rotation towards the orbit of mercury&quot; it may sound crazy to a modern secular neonate. In the WOD, however, that alignment of crystals produces a resonance associated with spirits of light. A resonance whose influence on the vampire makes him better able to resist daysleep. So the students of Mr. Magus would learn the first Coil of the Mystery of the Ascendant faster and more reliably than scientific students who assume it's all just a matter of conditioning. <br /> <br /> I don't mean to be That Guy; it's just a game and you can play it however you want. It's just that when the stereotypical Dragon is a mix of Dracula, Dr. Frankenstein, and the Ghost Busters, focusing on the scientific side of the covenant writes off a lot of their core themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T08:54:00-07:00","id":592694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=592651#post592651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The disparities between science, pseudoscience, and mysticism are less clear cut than most people think. All are attempts to explain the world via internally consistent systems of thought. The real difference is just the assumptions you are allowed to make when formulating theories, and the language you use to describe said theories. Secular skeptics claim science makes no assumptions, but in reality it assume the absence of the supernatural. Pseudoscience uses the language of science, but is willing to make limited assumptions about the presence and relevance of supernatural influences (often while denying their supernatural nature). Mysticism tends to assume the significance of supernatural influences, makes untestable claims about the nature of such influences, and uses archaic language to describe such influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to disagree here, especially the 'science assumes the absence of the supernatural'. The big assumption that science makes is the absence of the unexplainable, with scientists often assuming the absence of the supernatural (there are religious scientists who believe in the supernatural). Psuedoscience is, in my view, incorrect theories about how something might work*. In the WoD 'spirits don't exist' might be considered pseudoscience by Mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, a Crone cultist assumes their goddess is what grants power to their blood magic. A Dragon pseudoscientist accepts that blood magic works, but either doesn't claim to know what powers it or describes the power source in terms of &quot;energy&quot;. A scientist assumes blood magic is impossible and must be some kind of trickery. The problem in the WOD is obvious; the scientist is wrong. A Dragon, as a vampire who frequents haunted houses and spirit loci, does not have the luxury of being a strict scientist. </div> </div> </div>When a vampire scientist comes up against Blood Magic, their first response it 'it's probably not magic'. Their second response is 'why does Flesh Graft Treatment fail if I perform it'. Their third response should be to develop and test a theory. Eventually the scientist is either on the wrong track completely or starts being able to work blood magic. But by testing his assumption of 'magic is wrong' he was able to add more to his scientific knowledge and possibly develop something new and useful. A scientist's response to blood magic is not 'lol, wrong it doesn't exist', but 'it's probably some kind of trickery, I should discover how this trickery works'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When Mr Magus tells his students to meditate in a circle of crystals aligned &quot;in a counterclockwise rotation towards the orbit of mercury&quot; it may sound crazy to a modern secular neonate. In the WOD, however, that alignment of crystals produces a resonance associated with spirits of light. A resonance whose influence on the vampire makes him better able to resist daysleep. So the students of Mr. Magus would learn the first Coil of the Mystery of the Ascendant faster and more reliably than scientific students who assume it's all just a matter of conditioning. </div> </div> </div>Assuming these scientific students have no reason to believe in the evidence regarding spirits. I think that neonates visit Wyrm's Nests might be in order to reduce the amount of time they spend denying that it's all just conditioning and easily explained by mortal science. If this is the reason behind why it works, and there is enough evidence for it to be beyond reasonable doubt, it is science. Including weird crystal arrangements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't mean to be That Guy; it's just a game and you can play it however you want. It's just that when the stereotypical Dragon is a mix of Dracula, Dr. Frankenstein, and the Ghost Busters, focusing on the scientific side of the covenant writes off a lot of their core themes. </div> </div> </div>Oh, I look at them and interpret them as magicians who apply scientific rigor, I was just giving an idea as to how to separate them from the Tremere more. Dragons are split between the ones who say 'it works, don't question it, just improve it' and those who say 'if I look into why it works, I can improve it'. I love them because they are mystical (I refer to the coils as blood sorcery in most discussions), but they don't just take the answer they're given. I'd hate to see what the Ordo could do with Cruac and Theaban Sorcery.<br /> <br /> *not that it always does work, see homeopathy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T13:00:36-07:00","id":594921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=591216#post591216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conceptual difference between the Tremere and the Odo Dracul isn't superstition vs science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so's we all knows: THIS is a difference that *I* invented for MY game, not something that comes out of the 'canon' of either game, <b>Requiem</b> or <b>Masquerade</b>. Here's what I wrote about this for my own game:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, the Tremere are mystics who dabble in science and the Ordo Dracul are scientists how dabble in the mystical, but what does that mean? The answer is twofold.<br /> <br /> First, the ENDS to which each Covenant applies their arts differ tremendously. The Tremere seek power for the sake of power, wishing only to harness the potential of their Vitae as vampires, all in order to achieve individual goals. On the other hand, the Dragons seek to transcend their undead state, and only after that has come about do they expect a reward for their altered nature. The Tremere think in the very short-term \u2013 at least insofar as vampires see it \u2013 while the Order plays a much longer game. Of course, a character in either Covenant shall approach these truths however she sees fit, but we\u2019re speaking in generalities here.<br /> <br /> The second part is the APPROACH that each Covenant takes. The Dragons see themselves as investigators, as rational beings who must sometimes use irrational methods, but the Tremere claim a legacy of magic, which they may augment with modern scientific tools. The net effect of these differences is negligible on the street-level, but membership in a Covenant ultimately boils down to accepting and acting out the party line. Calling a mystic a scientist or vice versa sounds like fighting words to any Kindred who takes her work seriously. </div> </div> </div>...As far as how MUCH of a difference there really is, that's debatable. I wanted some kind of REASON why the Dragons were different from the Warlocks, and I did that by cranking the contrast between them up to eleven.<br /> <br /> I don't offer the above to invalidate anything that rest of you have stated or suggested or whatnot. I'm only making my OWN version clear, not saying that anyone needs to agree. Heck, I quite like it when I'm able to debate stuff that I'm actually wrong about, so please do carry on! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T13:11:23-07:00","id":594926,"title":"","content":"Oh, and since someone asked, there's the 'elevator speech' for how my <b>Requiem</b> Thaumaturgy blood magic works:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Standing somewhere between the witcheries of Cr\u00faac and the examinations of the Dragons\u2019 Mysteries, Thaumaturgy uses Vitae to focus power through a vampire, something only possible with a strong will, a disciplined mind, and proper study.<br /> \u2022 Uses a series of elemental Paths that increase in potency<br /> \u2022 Each Path allows access to a series of Sendings, effects that must be meticulously prepared and cast; functionally more akin to Coils and Scales of the Dragon, respectively, than other Blood Sorcery, but far more mystical in nature<br /> \u2022 Thaumaturgy is alien and anathema to the Blood Sorceries of Cr\u00faac and Theban Sorcery; the two types of blood magic cannot exist within one Kindred, and tales of what comes from those who attempt such are as gruesome as they are secret<br /> \u2022 Due to similar roots, Thaumaturgy Paths and Coils of the Dragon may have SOME limited compatibility, but since the two factions who use these respective arts are dire enemies, no known collaboration has ever been recorded<br /> \u2022 Thaumaturgy demands great focus and attention to use, and the consequences of failure are often spectacular </div> </div> </div>I'm still hammering out solid mechanics with playtesting, but that's where it starts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T07:35:51-07:00","id":596955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phaolan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=594921#post594921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just so's we all knows: THIS is a difference that *I* invented for MY game, not something that comes out of the 'canon' of either game, <b>Requiem</b> or <b>Masquerade</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, while it's not explicitly stated in canon, the inner-control vs outer-control disparity as I described it is strongly rooted in the canonical descriptions of both organizations. True, it's not completely black and white, there is overlap. Tremere sorcerers no doubt sought ways to overcome the downsides of the curse, and Draculan mystics aren't shy about asserting power over the world around them. However, the point of the Ordo Dracul is to overcome the curse, where as the Tremere embraced the curse (pun intended) in order to gain mystical power. The Tremere paths are primarily focused on manipulating the external world, while the Coils/Mysteries of the dragon are focused on manipulating the dragon's own state. <br /> <br /> Canon doesn't directly address this disparity, because the two organizations don't co-exist in canonical sources. Still, it's hardly surprising that once you started mixing them together, you came to the same conclusions about their differences that I did in my comments. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T04:05:49-07:00","id":604583,"title":"","content":"Hi, this is a response to Aermas question posted on 05-13-2014.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/134959-converting-a-tremere-lawyer\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/134959-converting-a-tremere-lawyer\"> Converting a Tremere Lawyer - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/134959-converting-a-tremere-lawyer\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/134959-converting-a-tremere-lawyer </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> What is the best Bloodline/Clan to represent what used to be a Tremere Lawyer? I want Auspex Dominate &amp;amp; Blood Magic with strong political/social leanings, but I'm kinda lost on the Requiem lore. There seems to be a lot of ways to do blood magic now &amp;amp; most of the clans are gone or have been </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This is pretty in line with your question.<br /> <br /> He (or She, no idea really) asked: What is the best Bloodline/Clan to represent what used to be a Tremere Lawyer? I want Auspex Dominate &amp; Blood Magic with strong political/social leanings, but I'm kinda lost on the Requiem lore. There seems to be a lot of ways to do blood magic now &amp; most of the clans are gone or have been assimilated. What do you guys recommend?<br /> <br /> Here is the response I gave on 05-20-2014:<br /> <br /> To Aermas, on converting a Tremere Lawyer to Requiem.<br /> <br /> The Tremere seem to be the most difficult to transfer from Mascaraed to Requiem. I will attempt to offer some help, or at least advice for conversion to Requiem, since I do not have Blood and Smoke. I will suggest going into a conversion mechanically first, then going into back story fluff secondly.<br /> <br /> The first question I would ask is do you want the Tremere to be a Bloodline or a completely separate Clan. Ultimately, I think the Tremere should be whichever is easier for the storyteller to enter into their game.<br /> <br /> The second question I\u2019d ask is; what does the Tremere bring to the game that is appealing?<br /> <br /> Considering the Occult power differential between the Tremere and other Clans in Masquerade and Requiems pension for balance, there are several Bloodlines I would suggest working with to build a Franken-Tremere.<br /> <br /> The Geheim (p. 83-88) and the Corajoso (p. 102-104) Bloodlines from the Ancient Bloodlines Book, and the Architects of the Monolith Bloodline from the Bloodlines: The Hidden Book (p. 30\u201337), are the most Tremere\u2019y of the game builds I have seen without unbalancing the game.<br /> <br /> Personally I like the Corajoso Bloodline for entering the enforced close nit familial ties through Linagem without making weakness to Vinculum a Clan weakness. It gives you more room to play with character creation.<br /> <br /> The Geheim bring in more of a Victorian alchemical occult mad scientist feel to the game.<br /> <br /> Since most people seem to dislike the Architects, I think their Ritual Blood Magic: The Gilded Cage, should be given to the Tremere with a Clan/Bloodline status restriction.<br /> <br /> The Corajoso Bloodline Discipline Linagem is so potent that I think is should be used as a Dominate replacement in a Clan/Bloodline build. It also can\u2019t be purchased by Ghouls, so one more thing making the Vampire special.<br /> <br /> I like Geheim Bloodline Discipline Blut Alchemie as a good Animalism replacement in a Clan/Bloodline build.<br /> <br /> Using Linagem and Blut Alchemie as replacements for the Common disciplines helps make the Tremere seem separate from the Ventrue, more alien.<br /> <br /> The weakness should reflect this Alien nature as well. If you are going for the Bloodline build I would suggest the Corajoso Bloodline weakness to be layered on top of the standard Venture weakness. If you are going for the Clan build, I would say that the either using both the Geheim and the Corajoso Bloodline weaknesses as the clan weakness, or either of them in combination with the Derangement Fasination with the Occult.<br /> <br /> Since this has prattled on, I will go into the possibility of Fluff briefly. The family backgrounds of the Bloodlines work great for building the New Tremere backstory without relying on the Masquerade history so heavily tied to the meta-plot. The Geheim Bloodline history is good for the time frame and founding of the Clan/Bloodline, possibly fitting in that through Alchemy they stole their Vampirism like in the old WoD. The Corajoso Bloodline history work well for the function of the internal politics of the family. Finally the Architects Bloodline history of how they obtained the Gilded Cage Blood Sorcery would work well for secrets and baggage that the family would not like to get out, as well as general mistrust that could build between the Tremere Family and other Covenants.<br /> <br /> Good luck and I hope this helps.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2629-desbjm","name":"DesBJM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T13:40:56-07:00","id":604928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere#post581310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone!<br /> <br /> I was wondering, has anyone done anything with Tremere from V;tM? I thought they were awesome! Essentially vampire mages with the their discipline (can't remember the name) limited only by their imagination! I checked the Homebrew sticky, and tI haven't noticed anything there.<br /> <br /> Just curious. I thought they were pretty nifty <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Thaumaturgy, that's it =D</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Kind of lost the point of having an entire clan devoted to blood magic when we now have an entire faction of warlocks that any clan would be able to join.<br /> <br /> Though if I were going to recreate the Tremere, I could see it being done in one of two ways. First possibility is a Mekhet bloodline who became addicted to the secrets of the Arcane and have devoted themselves to studying as much blood magic as they can. Their power of Auspex being exceedingly helpful in furthering their research.<br /> <br /> The second option is a Ventrue bloodline who believe themselves to be the &quot;Magical Elite&quot; among the Circle and wish to restrict access to Cruac among the lesser clans while making sure they stand atop the covenant. Their power of Dominate matching well with the original Tremere's disciplines and keeping lesser Warlocks in their place.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, however, the Mage references that there actually used to be a clan of vampires named the Tremere, but they went extinct long ago, and the liches took the name for themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-27-2015, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T06:59:53-07:00","id":605552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/581310-tremere?p=604928#post604928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Kind of lost the point of having an entire clan devoted to blood magic when we now have an entire faction of warlocks that any clan would be able to join.<br /> <br /> Though if I were going to recreate the Tremere, I could see it being done in one of two ways. First possibility is a Mekhet bloodline who became addicted to the secrets of the Arcane and have devoted themselves to studying as much blood magic as they can. Their power of Auspex being exceedingly helpful in furthering their research.<br /> <br /> The second option is a Ventrue bloodline who believe themselves to be the &quot;Magical Elite&quot; among the Circle and wish to restrict access to Cruac among the lesser clans while making sure they stand atop the covenant. Their power of Dominate matching well with the original Tremere's disciplines and keeping lesser Warlocks in their place.<br /> <br /> <br /> If I'm not mistaken, however, the Mage references that there actually used to be a clan of vampires named the Tremere, but they went extinct long ago, and the liches took the name for themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting I been thinking about this and came up with a bloodline that could spawned from either the shadows or the Lords.<br /> In fact their origins are murky as most details about this minor covenant/ clan.<br /> <br /> Auspex, Dominate, Obfuscate, Fortitude<br /> Thaumaturgy follows Theban rules as it is more hermetic.<br /> <br /> Was the founder a mystic consuming kindred blood and who died and rose?<br /> Or were they the first mekhet revenants who diablarized some Ventrue(or vice versa)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}